    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4836           REVISED 06/17/09\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm a transportation\ncontract of the Canaseraga central school district\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill directs the State Education Department to reimburse the\nCanaseraga Central School District for a specific 2008-09\ntransportation contract.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 validates all of the acts taken by the Canaseraga Central\nSchool District in connection with certain transportation contracts of\nthe 2008-09 school year. Section 2 directs the State Education\nDepartment to consider such contracts valid and proper obligations of\nthe Canaseraga Central School District. Section 3 indicates that this\nact shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Canaseraga Central School District was denied transportation aid\nfrom the New York State Education Department in the amount of $3,556.\nThe department claimed that the reason for denial of a certain\ncontract was due to late execution of the submission of the\ndocumentation. All other legal requirements for the contract were met\nby the district.\n\nHowever, there are several mitigating factors that led to the untimely\nsubmission and late acceptance date. These included multiple contracts\nfor services for the same student, caused by a change in the daily\ncontract amount and change in aide services. The Canaseraga Central\nSchool District also experienced difficulty in procuring a timely\nsignature from the transportation company and had to resubmit the\noriginal documents several times Upon request from NYSED.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThe Canaseraga Central School District has been denied transportation\naid in the amount of $3,556.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
